/target

# Local, machine-specific config (absolute paths): never commit.
bevy-rui-mcp.config.json

# Temporary normalized meta staged inside dist/ while packing a bundle (removed afterwards).
dist/.bevy-rui-index-meta-dist.json

# Index bundles and the persisted index are intentionally TRACKED: `dist/bevy-rui-index-<version>.tar.gz`
# plus `dist/index-manifest.json` are the artifacts published as GitHub Releases and read by `fetch-index`,
# and `data/` is the persisted index that ships in-tree so `serve` works with no `bevy_rui` source checkout
# and no config file — a consumer needs only the `bevy_rui` package *name* and *version*. The persisted
# `meta.json`/`registry.json` and the bundled copy carry no source path (`rui_path` is cleared on write),
# so no author-specific absolute path is ever shipped. See README "Using a prebuilt index" for the flow.
# Any other `*.tar.gz` (scratch archives, vendored tarballs) stays out of the repo.
*.tar.gz
!dist/bevy-rui-index-*.tar.gz
